11. Permission Architecture 

USER → ONE ROLE → ROLE PERMISSIONS → MODULE ACCESS → CRUD PERMISSIONS → ACTION / BUTTON PERMISSIONS 

Team, Region, Department and Manager are separate User attributes and do not create additional roles. 

12. Key Developer Rules 

A user can have only ONE role. 

Role must be a single Lookup field, not a multi-select lookup. 

Region must be a separate master module. 

Do not create Service Category, Service Group or Service Type master tables. 

Rate Card is one user-facing module; pricing rows are repeating rows within the Rate Card. 

Pricing Basis must be a Lookup/Master. 

Unit should dynamically respond to the selected Pricing Basis. 

Rate Card and pricing-row changes must have a complete immutable audit trail. 

CRUD and specific business-action/button permissions must be configurable from Settings. 

Do not hard-code action/button visibility into individual modules. 

Team, Region and Manager are separate from Role. 

No Tax/VAT configuration is required for this MVP. 